      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T10:02:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the updates.\n\nInteresting that odex is unchanged when fully disabling horizontal class merging. I wonder if the good odex results for the same-file restriction could be due to the merge groups being very small (meaning we maybe get similar dex2oat optimizations as without horizontal class merging), whereas with full app-wide merging the merge groups often contain \u003e10 classes.\n\nI think moving forward with the same-file restriction is fine.",
      "parentUuid": "c51a2ab8_5d17ecff",
      "revId": "a1b8b9bab92826da0c162e766bc78c2a48ba428e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
